      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "text": "In the present case, the best argument for applicants would be that, in given set of circumstances,\noffences under Sections 406 and 420 I.P.C. may not go simultaneously, however, the said argument\nis neither mentioned in application nor stated by Sri Om Prakash Rai, learned counsel for\napplicants.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 502,
      "end": 801,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sections 406",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 618,
          "end": 630
        },
        {
          "text": "420",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 635,
          "end": 638
        },
        {
          "text": "I.P.C.",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 639,
          "end": 645
        },
        {
          "text": "Om Prakash Rai",
          "label": "LAWYER",
          "start": 754,
          "end": 768
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "text": "Since the applicants have approached this Court to invoke inherent jurisdiction, the Court takes note of impugned order and finds that summoning order is unreasoned as well as it is in the teeth of judgment passed by Supreme Court in case of Delhi Race Club (1940) Ltd. and Ors. Vs. State of U.P.\nand Anr., 2024 SCC OnLine SC 2248.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 803,
      "end": 1134,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Supreme Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 1020,
          "end": 1033
        },
        {
          "text": "Delhi Race Club (1940) Ltd. and Ors. Vs. State of U.P.\nand Anr., 2024 SCC OnLine SC 2248",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1045,
          "end": 1133
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "text": "For reference relevant paragraphs thereof are reproduced Gurpreet Singh Bhogal And Another vs State Of U.P. And Another on 13 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/112807140/\n1 hereinafter :-\n\"41.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1135,
      "end": 1353,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Gurpreet Singh Bhogal And Another vs State Of U.P. And Another on 13 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1192,
          "end": 1290
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 6,
      "text": "Before we close this matter, we would like to say something as regards the casual approach of the courts below in cases like the one at hand.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1354,
      "end": 1495,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "The Penal Code, 1860 (IPC) was the official Criminal Code in the Republic of India inherited from the British India after independence.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1496,
      "end": 1631,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Penal Code, 1860 (IPC)",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1500,
          "end": 1522
        },
        {
          "text": "Republic of India",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 1561,
          "end": 1578
        },
        {
          "text": "British India",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 1598,
          "end": 1611
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "The IPC came into force in the sub-continent during the British rule in 1862.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1632,
      "end": 1709,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "IPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1636,
          "end": 1639
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "The IPC remained in force for almost a period of 162 years until it was repealed and replaced by the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (\"BNS\") in December 2023 which came into effect on 1st July 2024.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1710,
      "end": 1900,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "IPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1714,
          "end": 1717
        },
        {
          "text": "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 1811,
          "end": 1834
        },
        {
          "text": "1st July 2024",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1886,
          "end": 1899
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "It is indeed very sad to note that even after these many years, the courts have not been able to understand the fine distinction between criminal breach of trust and cheating.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1901,
      "end": 2076,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "42. When dealing with a private complaint, the law enjoins upon the magistrate a duty to meticulously examine the contents of the complaint so as to determine whether the offence of cheating or criminal breach of trust as the case may be is made out from the averments made in the complaint.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2078,
      "end": 2369,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "The magistrate must carefully apply its mind to ascertain whether the allegations, as stated, genuinely constitute these specific offences.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2370,
      "end": 2509,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "In contrast, when a case arises from a FIR, this responsibility is of the police - to thoroughly ascertain whether the allegations levelled by the informant indeed falls under the category of cheating or criminal breach of trust.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2510,
      "end": 2739,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "Unfortunately,\nit has become a common practice for the police officers to routinely and mechanically proceed to register an FIR for both the offences i.e. criminal breach of trust and cheating on a mere allegation of some dishonesty or fraud, without any proper application of mind.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2740,
      "end": 3022,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "43. It is high time that the police officers across the country are imparted proper training in law so as to understand the fine distinction between the offence of cheating viz-a-viz criminal breach of trust.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 3024,
      "end": 3232,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 16,
      "text": "Both offences are independent and distinct.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 3233,
      "end": 3276,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 17,
      "text": "The two offences cannot coexist simultaneously in the same set of facts.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 3277,
      "end": 3349,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "They are antithetical to each other.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 3350,
      "end": 3386,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 19,
      "text": "The two provisions of the IPC (now BNS, 2023) are not twins that they cannot survive without each other.\"",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 3387,
      "end": 3492,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "IPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 3413,
          "end": 3416
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 20,
      "text": "The Court also takes note other submissions of counsel for applicants that dispute is essentially arising out of a Builders and Buyers Agreement and in case, there is any violation of condition, the appropriate remedy is to approach the Uttar Pradesh Real Estate Regulatory Authority.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 3493,
      "end": 3778,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Uttar Pradesh Real Estate Regulatory Authority",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 3731,
          "end": 3777
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
